 - Provider .5 registers a synchronous final drain on Architectury SERVER_STOPPED, after native stopping/player-quit producers. Queue flush ownership now uses a lock: periodic attempts remain nonblocking and reject same-thread reentry, while the final drain waits for an active worker and drains the remaining original prefix. Database monitor acquisition follows the existing queue-to-database ordering, avoiding waiting for a queue while holding that monitor. Failed/uncertain writes retain existing conservative retry/review behavior and an explicit shutdown error reports uncommitted counts.
 - Database/queue lifetime stays with the mod, allowing later server sessions in the same process. This does not introduce a crash spool, promise persistence after a failed final drain, or close/recreate repositories and JDBC state at each world stop. Process-kill/device-loss and MySQL remain separate acceptance.
 - Fresh :neoforge:build succeeds with Java 21 in a separate artifact checkout/cache. Actual provider/SQLite suite passes 109 checks, including the prior 93, active-worker/final-drain waiting, late ordinary/batch entries, exact parameters, nonblocking periodic attempts, idempotent repeated drain, locked/uncertain outcomes, same-process later admission and callback reentry. Native restart/regression evidence is recorded separately by the parent project. No production activation is included.
